{"t": 249.59, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "p_sshi_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails on minimum output voltage (S5, S6) because it cannot extract enough power to support heavy loads, especially when the open-circuit voltage is low. A Parallel-SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology is implemented to flip the voltage across the piezo capacitance Cp at every extrema, significantly increasing the energy harvested per cycle. A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output voltage to ~3.3V, preventing it from exceeding the 3.6V limit in light-load conditions (S3).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "p_sshi_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails on minimum output voltage (S5, S6) because it cannot extract enough power to support heavy loads, especially when the open-circuit voltage is low. A Parallel-SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology is implemented to flip the voltage across the piezo capacitance Cp at every extrema, significantly increasing the energy harvested per cycle. A Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output voltage to ~3.3V, preventing it from exceeding the 3.6V limit in light-load conditions (S3).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-05}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0005, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}]}}
